@page
@model ErrorModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Error";
}

<h1>Something went wrong</h1>
<p class="subtitle">The page could not be rendered.</p>

<div class="banner banner-bad">
    <p>
        The detail is in the application log on the web server. Quote this request
        identifier when reporting it: <code>@Model.RequestId</code>
    </p>
</div>

<p class="note">
    The most common cause is a schema mismatch: sql/22 and sql/24 must both be
    deployed, and the application pool identity must be a member of the
    <strong>crawl_reader</strong> role created by sql/25. Nothing in this
    application writes to the database, so a failure here has changed nothing.
</p>
